     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"rce_achieved is not reachable. Step 1: inject_jndi_string works, because input_sanitized=false, so attacker_input_logged becomes true. Step 2: trigger_jndi_lookup needs message_lookups to be true. It is false, which matches the deployed formatMsgNoLookups mitigation, so jndi_lookup_triggered can never become true. No other technique achieves it. Without it, resolve_to_attacker cannot fire, so attacker_endpoint_contacted, malicious_reference_returned and remote_class_loaded stay false. That holds even though the gadget path (gadget_present=true) would otherwise get around trust_url_codebase=false. execute_payload therefore never runs. One wording conflict: the model says a mitigation sets its constant true, while message_lookups is listed as false. I read formatMsgNoLookups as the setting that keeps message_lookups false.\"}"
    }
